# Client-Server separation and GUI (Forge 1.12.2)

## Physical Side vs Logical Side

| Side | Meaning |
|------|---------|
| Physical CLIENT | The game process rendering the world |
| Physical SERVER | Dedicated server process (or integrated server in single-player) |
| Logical CLIENT | Code running on the client that can ONLY observe/render |
| Logical SERVER | Code running on the dedicated server that manages world state |

### Rules

- **Never** call client-only code from a logical server context
- **Never** modify server-side world data from the logical client
- Use `@SideOnly(Side.CLIENT)` for client-only code
- Use `DistExecutor` or `FMLCommonHandler` for safe side-aware execution without annotations

## @SideOnly Annotation

```java
// Class-level
@SideOnly(Side.CLIENT)
public class ClientProxy {
    public void init() { ... }
}

// Method-level
@SideOnly(Side.CLIENT)
public void clientOnlyMethod() { ... }
```

## Proxy Pattern

Forge 1.12.2 uses a proxy pattern for client/server separation:

```java
@Mod(modid = MOD_ID)
public class ExampleMod {
    @SidedProxy(
        clientSide = "com.example.examplemod.client.ClientProxy",
        serverSide = "com.example.examplemod.CommonProxy"
    )
    public static CommonProxy proxy;

    @Mod.EventHandler
    public void init(FMLInitializationEvent event) {
        proxy.init();
    }
}

public class CommonProxy {
    public void init() { /* both sides */ }
}

@SideOnly(Side.CLIENT)
public class ClientProxy extends CommonProxy {
    @Override
    public void init() {
        super.init();
        // client-only init: register renderers, keybindings
    }
}
```

## GUI System Overview

```
Player interacts
      │
      ▼
Block#onBlockActivated (Server) ──► creates IInteractionObject ──► openGui (Server)
                                                       │
                                                       ▼
                                              Container + Slot pair
                                                       │
                                               Container.openGui()
                                                       │
                                                       ▼
                                                   Renders Gui
```

## Decision: Container/Menu type

```
IF interactable block with persistent data (machine, chest)
  → Container + Slot + IInteractionObject

IF just a simple interaction (no data)
  → GuiScreen directly

IF inventory with multiple slots
  → Container (for slot management and transferHandler)
```

## Container Registration

```java
// Register in FMLInitializationEvent
@Mod.EventHandler
public void init(FMLInitializationEvent event) {
    NetworkRegistry.INSTANCE.registerGuiHandler(MOD_ID, new GuiHandler());
    // or use new SimpleGuiHandler() if extending IGuiHandler
}

// IGuiHandler implementation
public class GuiHandler implements IGuiHandler {
    @Override
    public Object getServerGuiElement(int ID, EntityPlayer player, World world, int x, int y, int z) {
        TileEntity tile = world.getTileEntity(new BlockPos(x, y, z));
        if (tile instanceof MyMachineTile) {
            return new MyContainer(player.inventory, (MyMachineTile) tile);
        }
        return null;
    }

    @Override
    public Object getClientGuiElement(int ID, EntityPlayer player, World world, int x, int y, int z) {
        TileEntity tile = world.getTileEntity(new BlockPos(x, y, z));
        if (tile instanceof MyMachineTile) {
            return new MyGui(new MyContainer(player.inventory, (MyMachineTile) tile), player.inventory);
        }
        return null;
    }
}
```

## Container class

```java
public class MyContainer extends Container {
    private final IInventory tile;

    public MyContainer(IInventory playerInventory, IInventory tileInventory) {
        this.tile = tileInventory;

        // Add player inventory slots
        for (int row = 0; row < 3; row++) {
            for (int col = 0; col < 9; col++) {
                this.addSlot(new Slot(playerInventory, col + row * 9 + 9,
                    8 + col * 18, 84 + row * 18));
            }
        }

        // Add player hotbar
        for (int col = 0; col < 9; col++) {
            this.addSlot(new Slot(playerInventory, col, 8 + col * 18, 142));
        }

        // Add tile inventory slots
        for (int row = 0; row < 3; row++) {
            for (int col = 0; col < 3; col++) {
                this.addSlot(new Slot(tileInventory, col + row * 3,
                    62 + col * 18, 17 + row * 18));
            }
        }
    }

    @Override
    public ItemStack transferStackInSlot(EntityPlayer player, int index) {
        ItemStack stack = ItemStack.EMPTY;
        Slot slot = this.inventorySlots.get(index);

        if (slot != null && slot.getHasStack()) {
            ItemStack stack1 = slot.getStack();
            stack = stack1.copy();

            if (index < 36) {
                // Player inventory → Tile
                if (!this.mergeItemStack(stack1, 36, this.inventorySlots.size(), true)) {
                    return ItemStack.EMPTY;
                }
            } else {
                // Tile → Player inventory
                if (!this.mergeItemStack(stack1, 0, 36, false)) {
                    return ItemStack.EMPTY;
                }
            }

            if (stack1.isEmpty()) {
                slot.putStack(ItemStack.EMPTY);
            } else {
                slot.onSlotChanged();
            }
        }

        return stack;
    }

    @Override
    public boolean canInteractWith(EntityPlayer player) {
        return tile.isUsableByPlayer(player);
    }
}
```

## GuiScreen (CLIENT ONLY)

```java
@SideOnly(Side.CLIENT)
public class MyGui extends GuiScreen {
    private final Container container;
    private final IInventory playerInventory;

    public MyGui(Container container, IInventory playerInventory) {
        this.container = container;
        this.playerInventory = playerInventory;
    }

    @Override
    public void drawScreen(int mouseX, int mouseY, float partialTicks) {
        this.drawDefaultBackground();
        super.drawScreen(mouseX, mouseY, partialTicks);
        this.renderHoveredToolTip(mouseX, mouseY);
    }

    @Override
    protected void drawGuiContainerBackgroundLayer(float partialTicks, int mouseX, int mouseY) {
        drawRect(x, y, x + 176, y + 166, 0xFF000000);
        // Draw slots, progress bars, etc.
    }

    @Override
    protected void mouseClicked(int mouseX, int mouseY, int mouseButton) throws IOException {
        super.mouseClicked(mouseX, mouseY, mouseButton);
        // Handle slot clicks
    }
}
```

## Opening the GUI

```java
// From a block's onActivated
@Override
public boolean onBlockActivated(World world, BlockPos pos, IBlockState state,
                                EntityPlayer player, EnumHand hand, EnumFacing facing,
                                float hitX, float hitY, float hitZ) {
    if (!world.isRemote) {
        player.openGui(MOD_ID, 0, world, pos.getX(), pos.getY(), pos.getZ());
    }
    return true;
}
```

## Common errors

- ❌ Opening a Container on the server without registering GuiHandler → crash
- ❌ `GuiScreen` called on server → use `@SideOnly(Side.CLIENT)`
- ❌ `transferStackInSlot` not implemented → Shift-click does nothing
- ❌ Modifying world state in Container constructor → too early, use `onContainerClosed`
- ❌ Player slot index out of range → verify slot indices are correct
